  "target_statement": "For C² U with genuine Hessian sandwich κ⁻¹I≤D²U≤I, κ>0, r:NNReal, a>0 and u,y:E, W=U+r/2||x-u||² is (κ⁻¹+r)-strongly convex and (1+r)-gradient-Lipschitz. Its Gibbs weight is integrable with strictly positive integral and normalized tilt is a probability. The volume-normalized Gibbs law of W+||x-y||²/(2a) equals that of U+(r+1/a)||x-w||²/2 for w=(r+1/a)⁻¹•(r•u+a⁻¹•y); its updated condition number is (aβ+1)K/(aβ+K), β=1+r, K=β/(κ⁻¹+r). The updated normalized potential is also explicitly certified to be a probability law.",
